Subject: [PATCH] device: do not add a route metric penalty on failed connectivity check

NetworkManager adds 20000 to the default route metric of a device whose
connectivity state is not FULL. The RDK networkmanager plugin owns the
route preference between ethernet and wifi and changes the metric of
the wlan0 connection at runtime, so the daemon must not add its own
penalty on top.

Return 0 from _dev_default_route_metric_penalty_get(). With a penalty of
0 the l3cfg sees no change on a connectivity state update, so no
needless commit is triggered.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RDK specific, route preference is owned by the networkmanager plugin]
---
 src/core/devices/nm-device.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/devices/nm-device.c b/src/core/devices/nm-device.c
index ed840044c5..8aaeed9003 100644
--- a/src/core/devices/nm-device.c
+++ b/src/core/devices/nm-device.c
@@ -5244,9 +5244,11 @@ _dev_default_route_metric_penalty_get(NMDevice *self, int addr_family)
     NMDevicePrivate *priv    = NM_DEVICE_GET_PRIVATE(self);
     const int        IS_IPv4 = NM_IS_IPv4(addr_family);
 
+    /* RDK: no penalty. The networkmanager plugin owns the route preference
+     * between interfaces, so a connectivity state must not change the metric. */
     if (priv->concheck_x[IS_IPv4].state != NM_CONNECTIVITY_FULL
         && nm_connectivity_check_enabled(concheck_get_mgr(self)))
-        return 20000;
+        return 0;
 
     return 0;
 }
